      <memberdef kind="enum" id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914b" prot="public" static="no" strong="yes">
        <type></type>
        <name>verbosity</name>
        <qualifiedname>micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::verbosity</qualifiedname>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914ba73be252ca82217b1458a25e6b4e99f15" prot="public">
          <name>silent</name>
          <initializer>= 0</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>No console output; only the exit code is returned. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914ba556966c7830465dc4623d62e32cec31d" prot="public">
          <name>quiet</name>
          <initializer>= 1</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Displays only the failed checks and the overall session summary; the TAP reporter also displays one result line per test suite, counted by the plan, and the failed checks as comments. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914bafea087517c26fadd409bd4b9dc642555" prot="public">
          <name>normal</name>
          <initializer>= 2</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Displays test suite and test case results; the individual checks are shown only for failures, the passed checks being only counted. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <enumvalue id="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914ba2c7aea4237e25b4f8ee3b0bf77d6fed0" prot="public">
          <name>verbose</name>
          <initializer>= 3</initializer>
          <briefdescription>
          </briefdescription>
          <detaileddescription>
<para>Displays all results, including passed checks, for maximum detail. </para>
          </detaileddescription>
        </enumvalue>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The verbosity levels for test reporting. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1a809871d76f29309ed9c6fbd96d5a914b" kindref="member">verbosity</ref></computeroutput> enumeration defines the available levels of detail for test output produced by the reporting system. These levels control the amount and type of information displayed during test execution, allowing users to tailor the output to their specific requirements.</para>
<para>The level is selected with the <computeroutput>--silent</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>--quiet</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>--verbose</computeroutput> command-line options, or with <computeroutput><ref refid="classmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1runner__options_1aff30f0303a958a549a2f4b6e67db00d5" kindref="member">runner_options::verbosity_level</ref></computeroutput>; the default is <computeroutput>normal</computeroutput>. The console output is intended for the people who watch the tests run, while the optional output file is intended for the integration with other tools. The level affects only the console output; the output file always receives the full report.</para>
<para>The <computeroutput>quiet</computeroutput> level displays the failed checks, with the names of the suite and of the test cases that contain them, and the totals; the passed checks and the passed test cases are not displayed. To also see them, use the <computeroutput>verbose</computeroutput> level, or keep <computeroutput>quiet</computeroutput> and use an output file, which receives them. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
